.TH POLYFILL 2
.SH NAME
polyfill: init, initzbuf, clearzbuf, setzbuf, fillpoly \- z-buffered polygon fill
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "draw.m";
include "math/polyfill.m";
polyfill := load Polyfill Polyfill->PATH;

Zstate: adt {
	r: Draw->Rect;
	zbuf0, zbuf1: array of int;
	xlen, ylen, xylen: int;
};

init:      fn();
initzbuf:  fn(r: Draw->Rect): ref Zstate;
clearzbuf: fn(s: ref Zstate);
setzbuf:   fn(s: ref Zstate, zd: int);
fillpoly:  fn(d: ref Image, v: array of Point, w: int,
              s: ref Image, p: Point,
              zstate: ref Zstate, dc, dx, dy: int);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Polyfill
.RB ( /dis/math/polyfill.dis )
rasterizes convex or simple polygons into a destination
.B Image
with an optional software depth buffer.
It is shared by
.IR draw3d (2)
(for
.B fillpoly3
and depth-tested sprites) and by
.B wm/polyhedra
(see
.IR wm-misc (1)).
.PP
.B Init
prepares the module.
.B Initzbuf
allocates a
.B Zstate
covering rectangle
.IR r ,
including two integer depth arrays sized to the rectangle.
.B Clearzbuf
resets depths to a far value.
.B Setzbuf
writes every sample to the constant
.IR zd .
.PP
.B Fillpoly
fills the polygon whose screen vertices are
.I v
into destination
.IR d ,
sampling source image
.I s
with alignment point
.I p
(the usual
.IR draw-image (2)
convention).
The winding argument
.I w
selects fill style as in Inferno polygon helpers.
.PP
When
.I zstate
is
.BR nil ,
the call is an ordinary fill with no depth test.
When
.I zstate
is non-nil, each pixel's depth is computed from the plane
.IP
.I z
=
.BI (dc + x* dx + y* dy) / ZSCALE
.PP
using the fixed-point scale
.B Draw3d->ZSCALE
.RB ( 1<<20 ).
A pixel is written only when it is nearer than the stored depth, which is then
updated.
.IR Draw3d (2)
computes
.BR dc ,
.BR dx ,
and
.B dy
from a face when
.B fillpoly3
is used with z-buffering enabled.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
	polyfill->init();
	zs := polyfill->initzbuf(img.r);
	polyfill->clearzbuf(zs);
	polyfill->fillpoly(img, verts, 0, colour, (0,0), zs, dc, dx, dy);
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/math/polyfill.b
.br
.B /module/math/polyfill.m
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR draw-image (2),
.IR wm-misc (1)
.SH BUGS
The z-buffer is integer and shared; concurrent drawers on the same
.B Zstate
are not interlocked.
Very large rectangles allocate large arrays.
